{{- /* rotini man page template (default — edit freely). It renders the SAME per-command
       doc-data as help into a roff man page, the markup the `man` program reads: lines
       starting with "." are requests (.TH header, .SH section, .TP tagged paragraph,
       .nf/.fi no-fill, .RS/.RE indent), and \fB…\fR / \fI…\fR are bold / italic.

       Text from the spec must be escaped before it reaches the page, or a summary starting
       with "." or holding a "\" would be read as markup. Use:
         roff       one line of text (line breaks become spaces)
         roffBlock  paragraphs: lines escaped, blank lines become .PP breaks
         roffIndented  the same, with .sp breaks, for text inside a .TP paragraph
         roffLines  lines kept as written, for inside .nf … .fi
         roffArg    one quoted argument of a request such as .TH or .SH

       After rendering, rotini drops blank lines (in roff they are stray space, not
       paragraph breaks) and trailing whitespace, and ends the page with a newline.

       DATA: .PageName .Section .Source .Date .RelatedPages .Summary
         .Description .Invocation .Usage/.UsageDerived .Passthrough .CommandGroups[]
         .Arguments[] .FlagGroups[] .Cascading[] .Environment[] .Configuration[] .Stdin
         .Output .ExitStatus[] .Examples[] .SeeAlso[]   (.Stdin and .Output are nil when the
         command declares none). .Passthrough is the command's name when every word after it
         is passed through unparsed, else "". A command or flag group carries .Description,
         the paragraph the command's `groups` gives it.
         A flag or argument row also carries .Env (its environment variables, in lookup order) and
         .ConfigKey (its config key, set only when the command reads config files);
         alsoSetBy .Env .ConfigKey "\\fB" "\\fR" renders them as "also set by ...".
         Argument, flag, env and config rows carry .Constraints (the declared bounds, lengths,
         item counts and repeatability as a short note) and .Rules (the same as sentences,
         plus pattern and separator), and .Accepts (what a time input accepts beyond its type's
         default: a layout, relative times).
         Argument, flag, env and config rows carry .EnumValues: every value that is not hidden,
         in declared order, as {.Value .Summary .Aliases .Deprecated .DeprecatedSince .RemovedIn
         .ReplacedBy .Note}, nil when no value declares more than its spelling (.Enum always
         holds the values alone, hidden ones left out); listed .Enum .EnumValues leaves out the
         deprecated ones too. An argument row carries .Passthrough when it and every word after it are
         passed on as typed. An output carries .Stream when the command writes a stream of
         .Type, one item at a time. An exit status row carries .Name (its snake_case name, or
         "") and .Retryable. Command, argument, flag, env and config rows carry
         .DeprecatedSince and .RemovedIn; deprecation .Deprecated .DeprecatedSince .RemovedIn
         renders "deprecated since 1.4.0, removed in 2.0.0: <message>".
         Argument, flag, env and config rows carry .Description (the input's longer text,
         paragraphs separated by blank lines; roffIndented keeps it inside the option's .TP)
         and .Stability ("experimental", "beta" or "" for stable, as declared), and command rows
         carry .Stability. The page's own .Stability is the command's, inherited from its
         ancestors; stabilityNote .Stability renders the line saying what it promises. An exit
         status row carries .DocsURL, a link to more about the code, or "".
         The page's .Effects says what running the command does, as declared ("destructive,
         not idempotent, open world"), "" when it declares none; a flag row's .Effects says what
         giving the flag adds ("destructive").
         The root's page carries .Topics[] {.Name .Summary}, its help topics. On a topic's page
         .Topic is true: .Summary and .Description are the topic's, .Environment holds a
         generated environment topic's rows, each with .Commands (the commands that read it),
         and the rest is empty.
       HELPERS: roff, roffBlock, roffIndented, roffLines, roffArg, join, upper, lower, title,
                trim, trimPrefix, trimSuffix, replace, indent, repeat, default, contains,
                hasPrefix, hasSuffix, first, last, alsoSetBy, deprecation, stabilityNote, listed,
                described. */ -}}
{{- define "notes"}}{{if .Required}} (required){{end}}{{with .Default}} (default {{roff .}}){{end}}{{with .Constraints}} ({{roff .}}){{end}}{{with .Accepts}} ({{roff .}}){{end}}{{with listed .Enum .EnumValues}} [{{roff (join . "|")}}]{{end}}{{with .Stability}} ({{.}}){{end}}{{if .Deprecated}} ({{roff (deprecation .Deprecated .DeprecatedSince .RemovedIn)}}){{end}}{{end -}}
{{- define "rules"}}{{with .Rules}}.br
{{roff (join . "; ")}}
{{end}}{{end -}}
{{- define "values"}}{{with .EnumValues}}.RS
.RS 2
{{range $i, $v := .}}{{if $i}}.br
{{end}}\fB{{roff $v.Value}}\fR{{with $v.Summary}} \- {{roff .}}{{end}}{{with $v.Note}} {{roff .}}{{end}}
{{end}}.RE
.RE
{{end}}{{end -}}
{{- define "description"}}{{with .Description}}.sp
{{roffIndented .}}
{{end}}{{end -}}
{{- define "flag"}}.TP
{{range $i, $id := .Identifiers}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}\fB{{roff $id}}\fR{{end}}{{with .Type}} \fI{{roff .}}\fR{{end}}
{{roff .Summary}}{{with .Effects}} ({{.}}){{end}}{{template "notes" .}}{{with .Implicit}} (implicit: {{roff .}}){{end}}
{{template "description" .}}{{template "rules" .}}{{if or .Env .ConfigKey}}.br
{{alsoSetBy .Env .ConfigKey "\\fB" "\\fR"}}
{{end}}{{template "values" .}}{{end -}}
